  m_Name: 6 Diagnose the Start
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Core.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Core.Editor.TutorialPage
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Diagnose the start
  m_Paragraphs:
    m_Items:
    - m_Type: 0
      Title:
        m_Untranslated: Diagnose the start
      Text:
        m_Untranslated: 'The <b>Diagnosis</b> tab checks what weighs on the start, in the editor, without a device: the settings of the project, and the content of the first scene of the build and of your playable scenes. List the scenes of your first playable screen under <b>Playable Scenes</b>, in <b>Project Settings › Startup Diagnostics</b>.


          A <b>Warning</b> has a clear fix whose effect is shown; an <b>Info</b> is a cost to look at. Each one says what it found and what to do, and lists what is in cause, such as the largest assets of a scene with the chain of references that pulls each one in. <b>Guide</b> opens its section of the optimization guide.


          With the measure you just made, <b>the checks of its longest step come first</b>, and each one shows the share of its step in the start. Turn on <b>Check Before Builds</b> in the settings to get the warnings in the console before each Android and iOS build.'
